WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.280
Hey Nina, what’s up?

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.600
Hey Tom, I’m working on a piece&nbsp;
about The Dark Knight Rises and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.880
it’s been forever since I’ve seen it. Can&nbsp;
you remind me what happens in that movie?

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.440
Sure. So it’s been eight years since all the stuff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.920
from “The Dark Knight,” and&nbsp;
Gotham is doing pretty well.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.080
Like, well enough that they don’t&nbsp;
need a rich guy dressed like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.920
bat to throw boomerangs at their problems anymore?

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.040
That’s exactly how well they’re doing, and&nbsp;
it’s all thanks to a little something called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.600
the Dent Act. See, Commissioner Gordon lied&nbsp;
to everybody and told them that Batman killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.960
Harvey Dent, and that because of that,&nbsp;
the police needed to be tough on crime.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.160
So they needed to be tough on crime because&nbsp;
the District Attorney got killed by Batman.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:30.686
Right.

00:00:30.686 --> 00:00:32.880
The fact that there was, like, a&nbsp;
clown army blowing up hospitals and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.000
taking hostages on boats did not convince&nbsp;
people that they should be tough on crime?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.960
I don’t know what to tell you, Nina.&nbsp;
People just love their district attorneys.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:39.600
I guess.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.760
Like, name the last five district attorneys&nbsp;
that you weren’t simply wild about.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:44.320
I can’t.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.040
Exactly. The point is that it worked, Batman&nbsp;
stopped being Batman, and Gordon -- Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.640
you know how sometimes when you tell an&nbsp;
enormous lie, the best thing you can do is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.920
to write down a damning confession and carry&nbsp;
it in your pocket with you wherever you go?

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:58.400
...No.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.080
Right, Gordon does that.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:00.640
Okay.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.600
And then meanwhile, there’s this guy&nbsp;
named Bane who’s out here kidnapping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.960
nuclear physicists and setting up&nbsp;
shop in the sewers under Gotham.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.960
That sounds like the sort of problem&nbsp;
that you would throw a boomerang at.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.400
And I can’t disagree with you, Nina.&nbsp;
The problem is that Bruce Wayne is all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.680
messed up. He’s walking with a cane&nbsp;
now ‘cause he ain’t got no knees.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.080
He… ain’t.... got… no... knees. Alright, go on.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.240
He’s got so few knees that he gets&nbsp;
robbed and beat up by Catwoman.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.360
Oh, okay. So Catwoman’s the bad guy?

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.480
No, he loves her.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.120
Okay.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.520
So then Gordon gets kidnapped by Bane, but he&nbsp;
gets rescued by a cop named John Blake who knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.600
that Bruce Wayne is Batman because he saw Bruce&nbsp;
Wayne one time and thought that he seemed sad.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:37.120
...Uh huh.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.840
Now you seem sad. Are you Batman?

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.400
Yes.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.640
That tracks. So John Blake convinces Bruce&nbsp;
Wayne to be Batman again even though he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.960
ain’t got no knees, and Bruce Wayne tries&nbsp;
to convince Catwoman to help him find Bane.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.080
Yeah, but why would he trust her? She robbed&nbsp;
him and then she beat the crap out of him.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.120
Yeah, but he loves her.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:56.240
Okay.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:57.680
So Catwoman betrays him.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.520
So Catwoman is the bad guy?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.080
No.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:00.560
Okay.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.040
She takes Batman to Bane and Bane breaks Batman’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.920
spine and then flies him overseas&nbsp;
and drops him down a metaphor.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.200
Well, sure. That happens.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.440
And then Bane takes Gotham hostage with a nuclear&nbsp;
bomb that he made out of an old Wayne Enterprises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.680
science project, but first he explodes a bunch of&nbsp;
stuff and then he tells everyone that the police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.440
lied about the death of Harvey Dent and that&nbsp;
there was no reason to be tough on crime at all.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.680
No reason besides the clown&nbsp;
army and the bazooka fights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.520
and the hospital bombings&nbsp;
from the very last movie.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.880
Yeah. Besides that.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:25.380
Right.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:29.840
So then Bruce finds out this whole backstory for&nbsp;
somebody that got out of the metaphor that he got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:34.240
dropped into one time and it sure shootin’ sounds&nbsp;
like he’s learning about Bane, on account of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:39.040
character having the same backstory as Bane from&nbsp;
the comics, but it turns out it’s not Bane at all.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.160
The character with Bane’s origin&nbsp;
story from the comics is not Bane?

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.320
No. It’s a twist.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:44.960
A twist.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.560
Yeah, a twist. Like, remember in “Batman&nbsp;
Begins” when the movie told you that a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:52.400
character had one name, but then twist, it&nbsp;
turned out that they had a different name?

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.280
Uh huh.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.400
It’s a twist!

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:54.960
Sure.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:58.880
So then Batman gets his spine punched&nbsp;
back together and makes a giant jump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.480
out of the metaphor that he’s been stuck in.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.320
Does he get his knees punched back together too?

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.160
… and he gets back into Gotham with&nbsp;
hours to spare before the nuke goes off.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.760
The clock is ticking.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:11.680
Big time. Yeah. So he draws a giant&nbsp;
bat symbol on a wall with gasoline and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.040
then waits around for a couple of hours&nbsp;
for an opportunity to light it on fire.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.320
So… No, you know what? I feel&nbsp;
like if I keep interrupting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:19.520
every time something doesn’t make sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:23.440
we’re never going to be done here. So Batman&nbsp;
is just lighting the city on actual fire now?

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.360
Sometimes in order to save that which we love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:29.040
we must first set it on fire.&nbsp;
It’s like when my mom got sick...

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:29.840
Nope. Got it.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.080
So then Batman asks Catwoman for help.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.480
Because she’s … wait, why?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.960
And then they go to stop Bane, but then it turns&nbsp;
out that Batman’s old girlfriend Miranda Tate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:44.400
is actually in charge of the whole operation&nbsp;
because she is secretly Talia Al Ghul.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:44.960
What?

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:48.080
It’s a twist. Like remember in&nbsp;
Batman Begins where the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.920
told you that a character had one name, but it…
 

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:50.400
I remember.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.560
And how earlier in this movie, they told you that&nbsp;
someone had one name, but it turned out that...

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:54.960
Right.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.760
A twist is when someone has a&nbsp;
different name than you thought.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.800
So Catwoman shoots Bane with&nbsp;
a great big gun and kills him.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.000
So Catwoman’s the bad g…

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.680
Talia crashes her car, she dies, and&nbsp;
Batman winches the bomb that’s about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:10.080
to go off to the back of his airplane, flies&nbsp;
it out over the ocean and then he dies too.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.600
Oh bummer. Thanks for your h…

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.840
Or does he?

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:14.600
F---

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.480
‘Cause later on, we find out that Catwoman&nbsp;
and Batman are secretly living in Italy eating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.800
biscotti every day and waiting for Alfred&nbsp;
to show up so they can ruin his vacation.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.760
...is that a twist?

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:28.320
Oh ho ho, yeah. It’s a big one. And&nbsp;
if you think that’s a good twist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.440
wait until you find out what happens&nbsp;
with that John Blake fella from earlier.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:34.960
What happens with him?

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.080
BIG old twist.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.400
Oh… God.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.560
Yeah, you remember what a twist is, don’t you?&nbsp;
It’s what happens when somebody who you think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:47.840
has one name actually has a different name.&nbsp;
It’s like in “Batman Begins,” when… hello?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:55.840
Hello? Nina, are you there? Nina?

